description:
Now that we're on Java 21, the 3 daemon threads in BridgeClient.java (MCP-Server, Stdin-Watcher, Potato-Ping) can use Thread.ofVirtual() instead of manual Thread + setDaemon(true). Virtual threads are always daemon-like, so setDaemon calls go away too.

Example:
```java
// Before
Thread mcpThread = new Thread(() -> mcpServer.start(mcpPort), "MCP-Server");
mcpThread.setDaemon(true);
mcpThread.start();

// After
Thread.ofVirtual().name("MCP-Server").start(() -> mcpServer.start(mcpPort));
```

Small change, 3 sites in BridgeClient.java. Low risk.
